|CKBPriest of Set|000

|CK0Priests of Set are evil ritualists who wield curses, darkness, decay,
coercion, and death. Their ceremonial dagger anchors a hostile divine toolkit
that is intentionally very different from Mitra's protective faith.|000

|CKBHow it plays|000
|CK0A Priest manages dark conviction and pacts while weakening enemies before
the decisive rite. The guild mixes direct spell damage with afflictions,
life-draining, summoned aid, resurrection, and religious utility. Its powers
and identity require commitment to Set and an evil path.|000

|CKBCore skills|000
|CK0fragility opens defenses, dreadspike and gstrike deal damage,
anathema and objurgate condemn targets, leech steals vitality, familiar calls
dark assistance, mend and respite provide limited recovery, and resurrection
returns the dead under Set's influence.|000

|CKBBest fit|000
|CK0Choose Priest of Set if you want a sinister caster built around debuffs,
ritual pressure, resource planning, and explicitly evil roleplay rather than a
neutral healer in darker colours.|000

|CK0After joining, use |CKBpriesthelp|CK0, |CKBprayers|CK0, |CKBdfavor|CK0,
and |CKBdpact|CK0 for the complete doctrine.|000

